# A room on this computer for a CozyCast server elsewhere
# (docs/home-hosting.md). "./cozycast.sh connect <server>" copies this file
# to .env.node and fills in the answers; after a change there:
# ./cozycast.sh start

# The server's address.
COZYCAST_HUB=cozy.example.com

# Optional
# The name proposed to the admin, who can change it.
# COZYCAST_ROOM_NAME=home
# What the room starts with, until its settings on the server pick something
# else. For a weak computer: a smaller desktop or stream, a faster preset.
# Desktop size and frame rate.
# SCREEN=1280x720@30
# The stream: bitrate in kbit/s, size in percent of the desktop size, and
# x264 speed preset.
# STREAM_BITRATE=2500
# STREAM_SCALE=100
# X264_PRESET=veryfast
# Stream choices offered in the room's settings on the server (presets
# fastest first; faster presets use less CPU but look blockier at the same
# bitrate). Leaving one out here takes it off that list.
# STREAM_BITRATES=500 1000 1500 2500 4000 6000 8000
# STREAM_SCALES=100 75 67 50
# X264_PRESETS=ultrafast superfast veryfast
